# Nvidia's driver packages. They ship in a small side repository next to the
# system image instead of inside it: about 2.4 GiB installed, and needed only on
# machines with an Nvidia card.
#
# build.sh resolves each driver flavour against the image's own package
# database, so the repository holds only what the image lacks. The installer
# installs one flavour, from that repository, offline, and only when the user
# chose an Nvidia driver.
#
# Keep in step with installer/sys/gpu.go (NvidiaPackages), which picks the
# flavour, and with build_nvidia_repo in build.sh, which resolves them.

nvidia-open
nvidia-open-dkms
nvidia-utils
egl-wayland

# What lets DKMS rebuild nvidia-open-dkms on every kernel upgrade.
linux-headers
